From a young age Norm has never shied away from asking the deep questions, not
only of himself, but of others he's been close to. Having a powerful connection
to Hamlet's, "This above all else, to thine own self be true," Norm has always
tried to meaningfully uncover who his own true self is.

With an understanding that we all wear many faces in different settings, and
experience watching the transformation in himself and others even from a simple
change of clothes, or environment. Norm is experienced at helping to sort through
the different faces and layers and levels of inner confusion to help you to
see your real core self.

What's holding you back from being who you really want to be?




